# File: hooks/register.test.ts
# Generated from: specs/541-run-an-nmg-sdlc-command-whose-text-arrives-as-a-pasted-prompt-instead-of-sending-it-to-the-model-as-plain-text/requirements.md
Feature: Pasted nmg-sdlc command text runs the command

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A pasted multi-line /sdlc-draft-issue runs as the command
    Given an interactive session with the hooks module loaded
    When a person-originated prompt with no engine-parsed command has text beginning "/sdlc-draft-issue" followed by a multi-line description
    Then the prompt is not sent to the model
    And /sdlc-draft-issue renders its workflow with the full remaining text as its arguments and enters plan mode

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Typed commands, plugin and meta prompts, and non-matching text pass through
    Given an interactive session with the hooks module loaded
    When a prompt is a typed slash command, a plugin-submitted or isMeta prompt, "/sdlc-unknown x", text mentioning "/sdlc-draft-issue" mid-text, or "/sdlc-draft-issuex y"
    Then the prompt reaches the engine unchanged with no workflow rendered
    And a person-originated prompt still ends an active model override

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A pasted interactive command in a headless session gets the typed refusal
    Given a headless session
    When a person-originated prompt's text begins with "/sdlc-draft-issue"
    Then the prompt is not sent to the model
    And the outcome is the "Run /sdlc-draft-issue in the TUI." refusal with no workflow rendered
